@startuml
title What is public and what is private

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Public state — on chain, readable by anyone" #FDF4F4 {
  component "total_supply\nmoves visibly on every mint and burn" as TS
  component "roles\nrole -> address -> bool" as Roles
  component "pause / deactivated\nPublicMutable" as P
  component "name, symbol, decimals\nPublicImmutable" as Meta
  component "terms, tokenId" as Terms
  component "freeze flags, list flags,\noperations switch, issuer_address\nDelayedPublicMutable" as Delayed
  component "public_balances\nonly when public_side_enabled = true" as PB
  component "roles_delay\nthe current delay, PublicMutable" as RD
}

package "Private state — notes in each holder's own PXE" #F4F8FC {
  component "balance of holder A\na set of UintNotes" as BA
  component "balance of holder B" as BB
  component "issuer's audit copies\ndelivered offchain" as IC
}

note as N1
  A balance is not a storage slot. It is the sum of the
  holder's own notes, which only that holder can spend —
  spending needs their nullifier key. That is why there is
  no forced transfer and no forced burn: the issuer can
  READ a balance from its copies, but cannot MOVE it.
end note
BA .. N1

note as N2
  Only the DelayedPublicMutable values can be read from a
  private function. Everything else in the public column is
  reachable only from a public function, which is why the
  pause check has to run in the enqueued public half.
end note
Delayed .. N2

note as N3
  public_balances exists only if the issuer deployed with
  public_side_enabled = true. It is the landing and departure point of
  the four AIP-20 bridges: a holder who uses one publishes its own side
  of that move, by choice. With the flag false every bridge reverts and
  the token is fully private.
end note
PB .. N3

@enduml
